### `work_orders.dispatch`: assign tech-north, set the slot, move to `scheduled` AND book the visit — one unit
### 2027-03-01 09:00 UTC is 10:00 in Bratislava, inside the customer's 07:00-19:00.
# @name DispatchWo7001
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
POST {{fshBaseUrl}}/commands/work-orders/{{Wo7001Id}}/dispatch
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Idempotency-Key: dispatch-7001
Content-Type: application/json

{ "technicianId": "{{userTechNorth}}", "startsAt": "2027-03-01T09:00:00Z", "durationMinutes": 90 }

### The dispatcher's retried click, same key and same input: the first answer is replayed and nothing runs again
# @name DispatchWo7001Replay
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
POST {{fshBaseUrl}}/commands/work-orders/{{Wo7001Id}}/dispatch
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Idempotency-Key: dispatch-7001
Content-Type: application/json

{ "technicianId": "{{userTechNorth}}", "startsAt": "2027-03-01T09:00:00Z", "durationMinutes": 90 }

### The technician may READ WO-7002 (it is assigned to them) but the command's rule names dispatcher or admin
# @name TechnicianDispatches
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [403]
POST {{fshBaseUrl}}/commands/work-orders/{{Wo7002Id}}/dispatch
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyTechNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "technicianId": "{{userTechNorth}}", "startsAt": "2027-03-03T09:00:00Z", "durationMinutes": 60 }

### 20:00 UTC is 21:00 in Bratislava: the host's before-write hook refuses it inside the unit
# @name OutsideHours
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
POST {{fshBaseUrl}}/commands/work-orders/{{Wo7002Id}}/dispatch
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "technicianId": "{{userTechNorth}}", "startsAt": "2027-03-03T20:00:00Z", "durationMinutes": 60 }

### tech-north is on WO-7001 from 09:00 to 10:30; a slot from 09:30 overlaps — the descriptor's exclusion refuses the visit
# @name DoubleBooking
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [409]
POST {{fshBaseUrl}}/commands/work-orders/{{Wo7003Id}}/dispatch
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "technicianId": "{{userTechNorth}}", "startsAt": "2027-03-01T09:30:00Z", "durationMinutes": 60 }

### The refused double booking left the job exactly as it was: the unit is all or nothing
# @name ReadWo7003AfterRefusal
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fshBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{Wo7003Id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### ... and booked nothing
# @name VisitsOfWo7003
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fshBaseUrl}}/api/visits?work_order_id=eq.{{Wo7003Id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### The refused out-of-hours slot left WO-7002 new, unscheduled and with no visit
# @name ReadWo7002AfterRefusal
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fshBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{Wo7002Id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

###
# @name VisitsOfWo7002
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fshBaseUrl}}/api/visits?work_order_id=eq.{{Wo7002Id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### The dispatched job, as stored
# @name ReadWo7001
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fshBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders/{{Wo7001Id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### ... and its visit — exactly one, though the command was sent twice
# @name VisitsOfWo7001
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fshBaseUrl}}/api/visits?work_order_id=eq.{{Wo7001Id}}
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
